B.ai3=new A.fC("1. Who we are","Tactivo is a football session-planning app operated by Tactivo Limited, company number 17373279, registered in England & Wales at 63 Carlton Road, Erith, DA8 1DX, United Kingdom. Contact us at info@tactivo.co.uk. By using Tactivo you agree to these terms.")
B.aik=new A.fC("2. Who can use it","You must be at least 16 to create an account. Tactivo is built for coaches, not for players: do not use it to store information about children or any other person.")
B.aih=new A.fC("3. Your account","Keep your password to yourself; you are responsible for what happens under your account. Tell us straight away if you think someone else has access to it.")
B.aic=new A.fC("4. Sessions and drills","Session plans are assembled on your device from a library of coach-written drills. They are suggestions, not instructions. You are the coach: you decide what is safe and appropriate for the players in front of you, and you remain responsible for their safety, supervision and wellbeing.")
B.aig=new A.fC("5. Drills you write","Drills and notes you write stay yours. You give us permission to store them and show them back to you inside the app, and nothing more \u2014 we do not publish them or show them to other coaches.")
B.ain=new A.fC("6. What you may not do","Do not use Tactivo unlawfully, do not try to break into or disrupt it, and do not copy the drill library out of the app to republish it elsewhere.")
B.aij=new A.fC("7. Cost","Tactivo is free to use. If we ever introduce paid features we will say so clearly beforehand, and anything you have already saved will stay accessible to you.")
B.aif=new A.fC("8. Ending it","You can delete your account at any time in Settings, which erases your data immediately. We may suspend an account that breaks these terms.")
B.aib=new A.fC("9. Our liability","Tactivo is provided as it is, without a promise that it will always be available or error-free. Nothing in these terms limits our liability for death or personal injury caused by negligence, for fraud, or for anything else that cannot be limited by law.")
B.ai5=new A.fC("10. Changes and law","We may update these terms and will change the date above when we do. They are governed by the law of England and Wales.")
B.avc=s([B.ai3,B.aik,B.aih,B.aic,B.aig,B.ain,B.aij,B.aif,B.aib,B.ai5],t.J8)
B.ai1=new A.a4V(B.avc)
B.ai_=new A.NL(B.ai1,null)
B.ail=new A.fC("1. Who is responsible","Tactivo Limited, company number 17373279, registered in England & Wales at 63 Carlton Road, Erith, DA8 1DX, United Kingdom, is the data controller for the information described here. Contact us at info@tactivo.co.uk about anything in this policy.")
B.aie=new A.fC("2. What we collect","Your email address and password, which is stored scrambled so nobody \u2014 including us \u2014 can read it. Your profile: display name, username, and anything optional you choose to add such as a photo, bio, location, phone number, coaching role, qualification or experience. Your coaching content: session plans, saved and self-written drills, session dates, team settings, and the ratings and private notes you leave after a session. If you answer it, how you heard about Tactivo. When you open the app, when you sign in, and at three points while you are first setting up \u2014 the welcome screen, the end of the questions, and the first session we show you \u2014 we record the moment, whether it was the iPhone app or the web, a random identifier for this install, and, once you have one, which account. Nothing else, so we can see whether Tactivo is being used. The set-up steps happen before you have an account, so those carry the install identifier alone, which is not linked to you and goes when the app does. If a 3D drill fails to load, the app sends us a problem report: what went wrong, which drill, how long it waited, the 3D player's last internal steps, and your account if you are signed in. It contains nothing you wrote, and we use it only to fix the fault.")
B.ai7=new A.fC("3. What we do not collect","Beyond the app-open, sign-in and set-up record and the 3D problem reports above, Tactivo has no analytics tools, no advertising and no tracking across other apps or websites. We do not record which screens you open or which features you use, we do not track your location, and we do not collect information about players or any other person. The app stores a sign-in token on your device so you stay signed in; it is not used to track you.\n\nWe do send email. Sign-in codes and messages about your own sessions go to every coach. Coaching tips and news go only to coaches who ticked the box, and you can untick it in Settings or use the unsubscribe link in any of those emails. Both kinds are sent through Resend, our email provider. For each message we record that it was sent, whether it arrived, whether it was opened (a tiny image in the email tells us), whether a link in it was tapped, and whether that tap reached what it promised. We also keep your time zone and country so that a message arrives at a sensible local hour. The same goes for phone notifications if you turn them on. We use this to send less, not more: it is how we cap tips at two emails a week and drop any message coaches ignore. Roughly one coach in seven, chosen at random and permanently, gets sign-in codes and session messages only, so we can tell whether the rest are worth sending.")
B.aia=new A.fC("4. Why we hold it","To give you the account and the app you asked for \u2014 building your sessions, keeping your library, and showing your season back to you. That is the contract between us. We also keep it secure, which is our legal obligation.")
B.aid=new A.fC("5. Who else sees it","Your coaching content is private to your account unless you send it to someone. Other coaches cannot see your profile, your notes or your ratings, and they cannot find your sessions; the only way anyone else sees a session is if you send them a link yourself, which section 6 explains. We use four suppliers to run the service: Supabase stores the database, your account and your photo, Resend sends our email \u2014 sign-in codes, messages about your own sessions and, if you ticked the box, coaching tips and news, OpenRouter runs the model described below, and Cloudflare serves the page a session link opens. Supabase and Resend hold the data in Ireland. Cloudflare serves that one page from wherever the reader is. If you sign in with Google or Apple, that company confirms who you are and tells us your email address. We never sell your data.")
B.ai4=new A.fC("6. Sending a session to another coach",'When you tap "Send to a coach" we make a link with a random twelve-character address and give it to you to send on. Anyone with the link can read it, with no account and no password, so send it to people you mean to send it to. It is not listed anywhere and we ask search engines not to index it, but it is not a secret either.\n\nThe link carries the session title, the age group, how long it runs and how many drills are in it, plus your first name unless you turn on "Share without my name". It carries the drills only as references to our own drill library, so the other coach\'s app rebuilds them from the copy already on their phone. A drill you wrote yourself is never sent, and nothing you typed on a library drill is either. Your email address, your username, your photo, your notes and your ratings never travel with a link.\n\nYou can stop it at any time. "Stop sharing" on the session, or on the drill, takes back every link you have made for it, and deleting the session or your account does the same. A link you stop may still be readable for up to a minute afterwards, because Cloudflare keeps a copy of the page close to readers to make it load quickly. Every shared page has a "Report this link" line that emails us, and we take down links that are reported for good reason.')
B.aim=new A.fC("7. The one thing we send to an AI service",'When you describe a session in your own words \u2014 "midfield gets overrun" \u2014 that sentence is sent to OpenRouter, which runs a Google Gemini model, to work out which focuses you mean. That is all it does: it never picks your drills, which are chosen on your phone from the library built into the app.\n\nWe send the sentence and nothing else. Not your name, not your email, not your saved sessions, and nothing identifying your account. We do not keep the sentence afterwards; we record only how large the request was, so we can see what the service costs. If it is unavailable your session is still built, from the words your phone can read on its own.')
B.aii=new A.fC("8. How long we keep it","Until you delete your account. Deleting it in Settings removes your account, profile, photo, sessions, drills and notes from our live systems immediately; encrypted backups age out within 30 days. There is no recovery, so export anything you want to keep first.")
B.ai9=new A.fC("9. Your rights","You can ask for a copy of your data, correct it, delete it, or object to how we use it. Most of it you can see and change in the app; for anything else email info@tactivo.co.uk and we will respond within one month. If you are unhappy with our answer you can complain to the Information Commissioner's Office at ico.org.uk.")
B.ai6=new A.fC("10. Children","Tactivo is for adult coaches and you must be 16 or over to use it. It holds no information about players. If that ever changes we will update this policy and tell you before it does.")
B.ai8=new A.fC("11. Changes","If we change this policy we will change the date above, and we will tell you in the app if the change is significant.")
